# The tolerance a rendered case must meet to PASS.
#
# max-diff     the largest per-channel difference (0 to 255) allowed anywhere
# max-bad-ppm  pixels differing by more than 1/255 in any channel, in parts per
#              million of the pixels
# evidence     the row of the oracle tolerance table that supports the pair
#              (documentation/conformance.md), or "none" while it is zero
#
# The tolerance is a finding, not a guess: shape-cpu's coverage is exact area and
# each oracle anti-aliases differently, so the pair is set from what
# `make oracle-tolerance` measures. Until a lowering exists to measure, it is
# zero, which only an exact match meets, so nothing passes by being loosely
# close. score.py fails on a nonzero pair whose evidence is "none".
max-diff	0
max-bad-ppm	0
evidence	none
